3. Added mock overrides for the actual hook imports
4. Simplified the component structure
5. Added all the necessary properties that the hooks typically provide
6. Added state management for the filter value

This approach should work better because:
1. We're mocking the exact hooks that the component tries to use
2. We're providing all the necessary functionality directly
3. We've removed the complexity of the context provider
4. We're providing proper state management for the filter value

The component should now render without the DataTableProvider error since we're providing the functionality directly through mocked hooks rather than trying to recreate the context system.

